! mcp_bootstrap_p141.strap -- the $RET return routine, second half:
! the SD (save/restore) path, the unstack path and the entry to
! MUP1, printed page 141.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.148, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID FA000047
!  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  141", rendered at 600 dpi.
! The column-heading row's own right-hand field prints
! "LOCATION  217206", which is line 1's address word.
!
! FIFTY PRINTED LINES AND ALL FIFTY EMIT BITS.  No comment card, no
! SYN, no DD, no DRZ, no reservation: this page is pure code, from
! 217206.00 to 217244.00, and the counter leaves it at 217245.00.
! (The volume survey OCR'd 34 rows and 217206.4C..217237.00.  That
! is a window and an under-read, exactly as the brief warned; see
! the agreement note at the bottom.)
!
! >>> FORTY-NINE CARDS, NOT FIFTY: LINES 1 AND 2 SHARE ONE. <<<
! The card-serial column, rendered at 600 dpi, reads FA000047 on
! BOTH line 1 and line 2, then FA000048 on line 3 and one per line
! to FA000095 on line 50.  48 + (50-3) = 95, so the run is
! contiguous and NOTHING FELL OFF THE TOP OR THE BOTTOM of the
! render.  The shared card was punched as a semicolon
! double-statement card -- "LVI,1,$+1.0 ; B,K SERCH" -- the same
! shape printed p.127 line 56 and printed p.136 lines 1-2 carry.
! The deck writes the two statements on two lines; the bits are the
! same and the oracle checks both.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BOTH JOINS ARE MEASURED, AND NEITHER REST ON THIS PAGE'S OWN INK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC. <<<  The "SLC,(8)217206.0" below is
! this page's line-1 LOCATION restated so the deck assembles
! standalone, and a hard SLC ASSERTS its value rather than checking
! it (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE
! WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER").  So both joins were read off the
! NEIGHBOURING PAGES instead, from ink, at 600 dpi:
!
!   BACKWARD.  printed p.140 (PDF p.147) ends at its line 48,
!   "48*  217205.40   217200.31 42   BXVZ, C P SNOW".  A half-word
!   branch at 217205.40 leaves the counter at 217206.00, which is
!   this page's line 1.  THE BACKWARD JOIN IS CLOSED.
!   (printed p.140 line 4 is its own "SLC,$" at 217155.00 -- a free
!   join witness for p.139->p.140, recorded here because it is the
!   only SLC anywhere near this page.)
!
!   FORWARD.  printed p.142 (PDF p.149) prints "LOCATION  217245"
!   in its column-heading row and its line 1 at 217245.00.  Line 50
!   here is a full word at 217244.00, so the counter arrives at
!   217245.00.  THE FORWARD JOIN IS CLOSED.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS, AND THE MANUAL THAT NAMES IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt ("The Logic of
! the Return Routine") describes THIS CODE, in order, and supplied
! four readings the drum could not:
!   "the return address is moved from the tentacle table to SICBU"
!       -- line 40, SV,$1,S IC BU, "-RET. AD. SET"
!   "the return address placed in the low register buffer (STIC)"
!       -- line 31, SV,0,ST IC
!   "return to the routine via the IF analyzer (MTC2A)"
!       -- line 35, BXVZ,MTC2A
!   "the unstack routine (KUNSTC) is entered"
!       -- lines 38 and 42
!   "control is given to MUP1 to attempt return to PP"
!       -- lines 9, 41 (M UP 1 is defined here, 217236.40)
! and the same document's program-status-table table prints
!   "SQK  .32-.49  Interrupt queue count"
!   "SSIO .61      SIO bit.  If 1, the program is in SIO mode."
! which settles lines 6, 34 and 41 -- see GLYPHS below.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin, and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed
! p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Names here may
! legitimately repeat names defined in pp.2-98 at other addresses.
! That is scope, not collision.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- FOUR QUESTIONS, FOUR ANSWERS, NONE OF THEM "IT LOOKS
! LIKE A C"
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE OPENS ITS ROUND GLYPHS CONSTANTLY. <<<  At 900 dpi
! line 16 prints its first half word as "COCCOO.CO 81" for
! 000000.00 81 and line 6 prints its second byte as "FC" for F0.
! A C cannot occur in an OCTAL field, so those are 0 with
! certainty; but per docs/transcription_workflow.md that is NOT a
! per-row ink gauge, so each of the four below was settled on what
! PRODUCED the characters, not on how they look.
!
! >>> THE !CHECK LINES BELOW CARRY THE RESOLVED READING, NOT A
! CHARACTER-BY-CHARACTER TRANSCRIPTION OF THE INK. <<<  Where this
! page prints "COCCOO.CO 81" the !CHECK says "000000.00 81", and
! where it prints "001000.CC FC" the !CHECK says "001000.00 F0".
! A later reader comparing deck against page will see the
! difference; it is deliberate and it is the only way the oracle's
! string comparison can run.
!
! (1) LINE 5'S LABEL IS "M D RET", WITH A D.  Two independent
!     printings agree:
!       (a) at 1800 dpi the second glyph has a STRAIGHT VERTICAL
!           LEFT STEM and squared top corners, and the SAME ROW's
!           operand "M C R" prints a round, stemless C a few
!           characters away -- the C/D discriminator of
!           docs/transcription_workflow.md applied within one row
!           off one drum;
!       (b) printed p.140 line 6 is
!           "217156.00  000000.31 89  217210.34 04
!            BZBZ,S AS($9),M D RET" -- a DIFFERENT page's print of
!           the same name, and its address 217210.34 is 217210.00
!           once the .34 operation bits come off, which is exactly
!           where line 5 sits.
!     MDRET is DEFINED here and referenced by no row on this page,
!     so within this deck it rests on ink alone; (b) is what takes
!     it off ink alone.
!
! (2) LINE 3 IS "B, C P SNOW", WITH A C, AND THE MANUAL SAYS SO.
!     docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt prints
!     "(CPSNOW) uses the JTSEXE subroutine to determine ..." in
!     typeset text.  printed p.140 line 38 then carries the
!     DEFINING CARD at 217200.00 -- "38*  217200.00  217201.03 01
!     C P SNOW  LVI,1,$+1.0  -CHECK FOR TS,EXE" -- read off PDF
!     p.147 at 600 dpi, which is where line 3's 217200.10 00
!     branches.
!
! (3) LINE 6 IS "SSIO", NOT "SSIC".  The last glyph is round and
!     open, so shape says nothing.  Three things settle it:
!     the manual's "SSIO .61 SIO bit"; the printed offset, which is
!     000000.75 -- 0o75 = 61 decimal, the manual's own bit; and
!     printed p.140 line 7, "BB,S SIO($9),C M SNOW", which prints
!     the name on a different page.  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap
!     line 10 already landed "SSIO SYN(BU,1), .61" with the comment
!     "-SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS"; THIS DECK USES THAT SPELLING
!     VERBATIM.
!
! (4) LINE 19'S MNEMONIC IS "CBZH", SETTLED BY THE ASSEMBLER AND
!     NOT BY INK.  Fed nine near-neighbours of the printed string,
!     strap_asm accepts exactly one:
!         CBZH   assembles, prints this page's own 217226.44 CA
!         CBZF CBZB CBZE CBZN CBZK CBZM CBZR CB2H C8ZH
!                "unknown mnemonic"
!     This is the eliminator of docs/transcription_workflow.md used
!     the way that file says to use it: it fired, and it is
!     decisive BECAUSE only one candidate is an operation.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ONE THING ON THIS PAGE I COULD NOT RESOLVE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 5'S COMMENT BANNER READS "S D RET" AND I CANNOT SAY
! WHETHER THE FIRST GLYPH IS AN S OR A WORN "$". <<<  The comment
! is "-**************S D RET*********".  At 1800 dpi the glyph is a
! clean curved S with NO vertical bar; a "$" on this drum is an S
! WITH a vertical bar, and a vertical stroke is the first thing
! this drum loses (same failure mode as B/8).  The reason it
! matters only a little and the reason it matters at all:
!   * MCP's pseudo-op codes are defined on printed p.43 as
!     "NULL $RET SYN,33.0" and friends, and the volume OCR reads
!     that very field as "D RET" and "S C RET" -- i.e. the OCR
!     cannot read a "$" there either.
!   * the typeset manual says the $RET routine "is entered at
!     CRETN", and printed p.140 line 5 IS "C RETN LVI,9,S PROG S",
!     so CRETN is p.140's label and MDRET is this page's.
! NO BIT DEPENDS ON IT: it is comment text, the row's label is
! settled independently (note 1 above), and the row's binary is
! checked.  It is transcribed below exactly as printed and is NOT
! resolved.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every one of the fifty line numbers carries the ordinary trailing
! asterisk ("1*", "50*"); that is the column, not a mark.  TWO rows
! carry a SECOND asterisk after their LOCATION -- line 14
! ("217216.00 *") and line 32 ("217231.40 *") -- the same
! unexplained mark printed pp.3/37/38/39/88/97/98/103/104 carry,
! and printed p.140 line 43 carries it too.  No mark changes a
! compiled bit; all four rows' bits are checked below and all four
! pass.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS, IN TWO CLASSES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! CLASS A -- PINNED BY A DEFINING CARD'S OWN LOCATION COLUMN, so
! the bit offset is READ and not conventional:
!   CPSNOW 217200.00   printed p.140 line 38, read at 600 dpi
!   MCR    215636.00   volume OCR "215636.00 ... M CR  XS IPL IN"
!   MC1    215637.00   volume OCR "215637.00 ... M C 1  DD(BU,24)"
!   MTC3A  215562.40   volume OCR "215562.40 ... M TC 3A"
!   MTC2A  215552.00   volume OCR "215552.00 ... M TC 2A  BB,..."
!   MR5    215645.00   volume OCR "215645.00 ... M R 5  DRZ(BU,64)"
!   MPP1   217260.00   volume OCR "217260.00 215636.22 ... M PP1"
!   MB1    217256.40   volume OCR "217256.40 ... M B1  M-1(BU,19)"
!   SICBU  215361.00   volume OCR "215361.00 000000.00+ S IC BU VF,0"
!   KSERCH 222020.00   volume OCR "222020.00 215021.23 K SERCH LVI"
!   KUNSTC 222037.00   volume OCR "222037.00 215021.23 K UNSTC LVI"
!   KINTTY 216010.40   volume OCR "216010.40 ... K INT TY"
!   MIFTTT 215666.00   DEFINED in decks/mcp_bootstrap_p121.strap
!                      line 5 at 215666.00, a landed page
!   SQK    .32  }      definitions landed in
!   SSIO   .61  }      decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap lines 9,10
!   STIC   215265.00   landed, printed p.116 header; the manual's
!                      "the saved IC is stored in STIC"
!   STLR   215230.00   landed, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap
!   SLRMCP 215362.00   landed, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap
!                      ("SLRMCP+9.0" prints 215373 on p.117)
!   MPRMQK 215640.00   landed, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p119.strap;
!                      p.120 line 6 is "M PRM QK DRZ"
!
! CLASS B -- back-derived from THIS page only: NONE.  Every symbol
! above is pinned by a card printed somewhere other than p.141.
! Where a value came from a printed branch or LV the bit offset
! would have been pinned ONLY TO THE HALF WORD (bit offsets 0-31
! encode identically); that caveat does not apply to any row here,
! and the half-word bit IS checked for all of them, because bit 32
! shows in the print (KINTTY .40 and MTC3A .40 and MB1 .40 would
! all FAIL if written .00).
!
! EVERY SPELLING ABOVE THAT ANOTHER DECK ALREADY USES IS COPIED
! FROM IT VERBATIM -- SSIO, SQK, STIC, STLR, SLRMCP, MCR, MC1, MR5,
! MPRMQK, MIFTTT, KUNSTC, KSERCH, SICBU.  tests/check_symbol_
! spellings.py passes with this deck in place ("1010 symbol
! definitions, no symbol spelled two ways").
!
! NAMES PRINTED WITH BLANKS are written closed up, as the deck
! format requires: "M D RET" -> MDRET, "M SD 2A" -> MSD2A,
! "S IC BU" -> SICBU, "ST IC" -> STIC, "K INT TY" -> KINTTY,
! "M C R" (line 5) and "MCR" (line 33) are ONE symbol printed two
! ways on one page.

KSERCH  SYN, (8)222020.0             ! line  2  "B,K SERCH"
CPSNOW  SYN, (8)217200.0             ! line  3  p.140 line 38 defines
KINTTY  SYN, (8)216010.40            ! line  4  "B,K INT TY"
MCR     SYN, (8)215636.0             ! lines 5,27,33  "M C R"/"M CR"/"MCR"
SSIO    SYN(BU,1), .61               ! line  6  p.109 line 10 verbatim
SQK     SYN(BU,18), .32              ! lines 34,41  p.109 line 9 verbatim
MC1     SYN, (8)215637.0             ! line 20  "M C 1"
MTC3A   SYN, (8)215562.40            ! line 30  "MTC3A"
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! line 31  "ST IC"
MTC2A   SYN, (8)215552.0             ! line 35  "MTC2A"
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0             ! line 37  "STLR"
SLRMCP  SYN, (8)215362.0             ! line 37  "SLRMCP"
KUNSTC  SYN, (8)222037.0             ! lines 38,42  "KUNSTC"
SICBU   SYN, (8)215361.0             ! line 40  "S IC BU"
MPRMQK  SYN, (8)215640.0             ! line 43  "MPRMQK"
MPP1    SYN, (8)217260.0             ! line 44  "M PP 1"
MR5     SYN, (8)215645.0             ! line 45  "M R 5"
MIFTTT  SYN, (8)215666.0             ! line 48  "MIFTTT-64.0" prints 215566
MB1     SYN, (8)217256.40            ! line 49  "M B1"

        SLC, (8)217206.0             ! line 1's printed LOCATION, and
                                     !   the heading row's "LOCATION
                                     !   217206".  ASSERTED, not
                                     !   checked -- see the join note.

        LVI, 1, $+1.0                ! line  1  card FA000047
        B, KSERCH                    ! line  2  card FA000047 (shared)
        B, CPSNOW                    ! line  3
        B, KINTTY                    ! line  4
MDRET   LX, $1, MCR                  ! line  5  -*****S D RET*****
        CM0000(BU,1), SSIO($9)       ! line  6
        LV, 4, 1.0($1)               ! line  7  -CHECK USERS TT
        BZB, .4($1), MSDA            ! line  8  -USER IS PP
        BXVZZ, MUP1                  ! line  9  -PRIMED OP
MSDA    LX, $2, 2.0($1)              ! line 10  -ADDR. OF USERS B,$MCP
        BZB, .6($4), $+1.32          ! line 11
        V+I, 2, .32                  ! line 12
        V+I, $2, .32                 ! line 13  -ADDR. OF USERS $OP IN $2
        SV, $1, $3                   ! line 14  -SENDERS K IN $3
        V+, 3, MX                    ! line 15
        L(BU,4), 0.0($1), -18        ! line 16
        V+I, 1, 2.32                 ! line 17
        LC, $2, $L                   ! line 18  -N IN C.F. $2
MSD2A   CBZH, $2, MSD3A              ! line 19
        V+, $3, MC1                  ! line 20  -GET NEXT RESTORE BIT
        V+I, $1, .32                 ! line 21
        BZB, 0.0($3), MSD2A          ! line 22  -NO RESTORE
        L(BU,32), 0.0($1), -32       ! line 23
        ST(BU,32), 0.0($2), -32      ! line 24  -RESTORE
        B, MSD2A                     ! line 25
MX      VF, .10                      ! line 26
MSD3A   LX, $1, MCR                  ! line 27
        BZB, .4($1), MIUP            ! line 28  -PP USER
        LV, $0, 1.32($1)             ! line 29
        SV, 0, MTC3A                 ! line 30
        SV, 0, STIC                  ! line 31
        LV, $1, 1.0($1)              ! line 32
        SV, $1, MCR                  ! line 33
        LV, 0, SQK($9)               ! line 34
        BXVZ, MTC2A                  ! line 35
MSD3B   LCI, 15, 30                  ! line 36
        T, 15, STLR, SLRMCP          ! line 37
        B, KUNSTC                    ! line 38
MIUP    LV, $1, 1.32($1)             ! line 39
        SV, $1, SICBU                ! line 40  -RET. AD. SET
MUP1    LV, 0, SQK($9)               ! line 41
        BZXVZ, KUNSTC                ! line 42
        LV, 1, MPRMQK                ! line 43
        BXVZZ, MPP1                  ! line 44
        LV, $2, MR5                  ! line 45
        LV, $2, 0.0($2)              ! line 46  -$OP CODE IN $2
        CM0000(BU,1), $2+.24         ! line 47  -MAKE OP CODE +
        LV, 2, MIFTTT-64.0($2)       ! line 48  -GET ADDRESS OF TT
        BB, .9($2), MB1              ! line 49
        L(BU,4), 0.0($2), -19        ! line 50  card FA000095

